Subject: [PATCH] bubblewrap: mount fresh proc as subset=pid

Keep a fresh PID namespace's procfs restricted to process entries. This avoids
revealing Docker's protected proc mounts while retaining task-local proc files.
Requires Linux 05dab768fc2dc7eb9b827201bb39bb5be54bce49 or an equivalent backport.
---
 bubblewrap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bubblewrap.c b/bubblewrap.c
index 9f5c54d5e3d0c..7a99f0b31a3e4 100644
--- a/bubblewrap.c
+++ b/bubblewrap.c
@@ -1387,7 +1387,7 @@ setup_newroot (bool unshare_pid)
             if (unshare_pid || opt_pidns_fd != -1)
               {
                 /* Our own procfs */
-                if (mount ("proc", dest_path, "proc", MS_NOSUID | MS_NOEXEC | MS_NODEV, NULL) != 0)
+                if (mount ("proc", dest_path, "proc", MS_NOSUID | MS_NOEXEC | MS_NODEV, "subset=pid") != 0)
                   die_with_mount_error ("Can't mount proc on %s", op->dest);
               }
             else
--
2.43.0
